{:edb/db-before-t 2285 :edb/db-after-t 2286 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535598 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:19:49.081Z" 13194139535598 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356877 13194139535598 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356884 13194139535598 true] [17592186119762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356870 13194139535598 true] [17592186120222 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535598 true] [17592186120222 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=4+3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2+6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x+5y+8z=229.\n$$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186120222 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: {x = 4 + 3t; y = 3 + 4t; z =-2 + 6tandΠ: 2x + 5y + 8z = 229$." 13194139535598 false] [17592186120222 1145 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y+8z & =229 \\\\ 2(4+3t)+5(3+4t)+8(-2+6t) & =229 \\\\ 8+6t+15+20t-16+48t & =229 \\\\ 74t & =222 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+3(3)=13 \\\\ y=3+4(3)=15 \\\\ z=-2+6(3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(13,15,16).$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186120223 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535598 true] [17592186120223 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=-3-5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-5y+3z-84=0.\n$$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186120223 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: {x = 5 - 2t; y =-1 + 4t; z =-3 - 5tandΠ: 2x - 5y + 3z - 84 = 0$." 13194139535598 false] [17592186120223 1145 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+3z-84 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-5(-1+4t)+3(-3-5t) & =84 \\\\ 10-4t+5-20t-9-15t & =84 \\\\ -39t & =78 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-2)=9 \\\\ y=-1+4(-2)=-9 \\\\ z=-3-5(-2)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(9,-9,7).$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356870 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356871 13194139535598 true] [17592186356870 1089 "q-108368" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356870 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535598 true] [17592186356870 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2t \\\\ y=-3+4t \\\\ z=5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+2y-z=33.\n$$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356870 1113 #uuid "3ee9813a-b1b3-5ef0-86f7-ac30b2000775" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356870 1145 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z & =33 \\\\ 3(4+2t)+2(-3+4t)-(5t) & =33 \\\\ 12+6t-6+8t-5t & =33 \\\\ 9t & =27 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2(3)=10 \\\\ y=-3+4(3)=9 \\\\ z=5(3)=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(10,9,15).$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356872 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356873 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356874 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356875 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356876 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1041 "selection" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356876 13194139535598 true] [17592186356871 1110 #uuid "85b5821d-cbb8-5c03-9816-ea997524331b" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356872 1034 "(20,29,40)" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535598 true] [17592186356872 1111 #uuid "42068190-cf84-57fe-bbaf-140c2463d46e" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356873 1034 "(-6,-23,-25)" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535598 true] [17592186356873 1111 #uuid "527a7770-d5f8-5a3d-8f3c-9ed5af2d3a60" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356874 1034 "(2,-7,-5)" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535598 true] [17592186356874 1111 #uuid "f5d807c9-264d-511a-9190-73c4168381a9" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356875 1034 "No intersection" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535598 true] [17592186356875 1111 #uuid "66f3bab9-e5a6-5f04-94ae-e823f168663e" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356876 1034 "(10,9,15)" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535598 true] [17592186356876 1111 #uuid "7e39da6c-a7b5-5af6-b99d-edf48043b61e" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356877 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356878 13194139535598 true] [17592186356877 1089 "q-108891" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356877 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535598 true] [17592186356877 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y}{4}=\\frac{1-z}{2},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩=-9.\n$$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356877 1113 #uuid "51708de4-81da-5999-acf1-9c92facc1391" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356877 1145 "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,0,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,4,-2⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,0,1⟩+t⟨3,4,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)-3(4t)+(1-2t) & =-9 \\\\ -8+12t-12t+1-2t & =-9 \\\\ -2t & =-2 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(1),4(1),1-2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(1,4,-1).$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356879 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356880 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356881 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356882 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356883 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1041 "selection" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356880 13194139535598 true] [17592186356878 1110 #uuid "a62b7884-84dc-538a-9bba-dca997f72e34" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356879 1034 "(-2,0,1)" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535598 true] [17592186356879 1111 #uuid "79a653c8-b4aa-594e-99f5-7bdd4b9ec4c0" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356880 1034 "(1,4,-1)" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535598 true] [17592186356880 1111 #uuid "b37cdbe3-b6af-5b8b-8187-a7041d20b8b8" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356881 1034 "(5,4,-3)" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535598 true] [17592186356881 1111 #uuid "6d2a8077-a027-5fd7-8c52-7fa90052e334" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356882 1034 "(4,8,-3)" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535598 true] [17592186356882 1111 #uuid "a9d396de-d5f4-5ba4-a270-d0a28f1f0cae" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356883 1034 "No intersection" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535598 true] [17592186356883 1111 #uuid "800ecb37-1966-513c-b261-63d50c33f347" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356884 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356885 13194139535598 true] [17592186356884 1089 "q-33987" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356884 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535598 true] [17592186356884 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,5,9⟩+t⟨4,-1,6⟩,\\,Π:-2x+4y+2z-16=0.\n$$" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356884 1113 #uuid "cbfd2820-3a30-53a2-832d-407032fe3cf1" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356884 1145 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+2z-16 & =0 \\\\ -2x+4y+2z & =16 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ ⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2(3+4t)+4(5-t)+2(9+6t) & =16 \\\\ -6-8t+20-4t+18+12t & =16 \\\\ 32 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356886 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356887 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356888 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356889 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356890 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1041 "selection" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356890 13194139535598 true] [17592186356885 1110 #uuid "2fb6d432-3990-5462-9174-0583dac17339" 13194139535598 true] [17592186356886 1034 "(-2,4,2)" 13194139535598 true] [1759218635688